OpenSSL-made fixtures (throwaway test keys, never used anywhere else):
streamed BER signature and envelope from `openssl cms -sign/-encrypt -stream -binary`.
ca.der: test root; leaf.der/leaf.p8: grace@example.net cert and key; content.txt: what was signed/encrypted.

oaep.eml is a synthetic Mail reader fixture for leaf.der / leaf.p8. The
inner text is "OAEP content from OpenSSL." OpenSSL CMS encrypted it with
AES-256-CBC and RSA-OAEP with SHA-256, MGF1-SHA-256, and the empty label.
